SpaceToggle OS is the AutoHotkey-era predecessor of Spaceadom
(https://github.com/nur-arpon/Spaceadom). It shares Spaceadom's idea and its
author, and from 17 September 2026 it is published under the same terms as
Spaceadom.

This is NOT an open-source licence. It is not one of the licences approved by
the Open Source Initiative, and it does not give you the rights that "open
source" usually implies (no right to redistribute, no right to sell, no right
to build a competing product on top of it). It is a source-available licence:
the code is public so you can read it, learn from it, run it yourself, and
verify what it does — nothing more.

